OL,3,GNEWSAWoman to run 200 miles for organ
OL,4,Adonation awareness
OL,5,
OL,6,FA woman who survived a rare
OL,7,Fpregnancy-related condition through a
OL,8,Fliver transplant is set to meet the
OL,9,Ffamily of the organ donor who saved her
OL,10,Flife as part of a week-long running
OL,11,Fchallenge.
OL,13,FLouise Prashad, who was 22 at the time
OL,14,Fand 37 weeks pregnant with twins,
OL,15,Fsuffered liver failure in 2016 and was
OL,16,Fplaced into an induced coma before
OL,17,Freceiving a transplant from 52-year-old
OL,18,Fdonor Sarah.
OL,20,FLouise is set to run 200 miles (322 km)
OL,21,Ffrom Birmingham to Bideford in Devon,
OL,22,Fwhere Sarah's family lives.
OL,23,APub: 30-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,388,380,200,160,0,100
